Crowdsourced, shot-by-shot. NOT a random sample of professional tennis: it
skews toward notable matches and top players. See reports/momentum_measurement.md
for what that costs the one analysis that uses it.

WHY THIS IS NOT IN vendor/. vendor/ is TennisMyLife match data under MIT, and
it is the model's only match-data source. MCP is a different source under a
non-commercial licence, read by exactly one measurement script
(scripts/measure_momentum.py). No MCP-derived number enters fitted_params.json,
model/, or any shipped artifact. If this project ever becomes commercial, any
conclusion drawn from MCP must be re-derived from a permissively licensed source.

The CSVs themselves are gitignored (93 MB); re-fetch them by running
  python -m scripts.measure_momentum
which downloads anything missing.

NOTE (2026-08-09): the source originally specified for this work,
JeffSackmann/tennis_slam_pointbypoint, returns HTTP 404 and that account is down
to a single public repository. MCP is the surviving Sackmann point-by-point
source, and it is the better one here anyway because it includes best-of-three
matches.
